<!--
  depth.dtd : how deep an instruction sits, and what the depth means.

  From the Depth mechanism study: a bracket label names what kind of
  instruction follows (SIGIL.label.roles) and quote depth names how it
  relates to its neighbours, a peer, a child, a grandchild
  (SIGIL.depth.roles). This subset binds the numbers: how deep depth may
  go, how each format marks it, and the refinement rule. Included by any
  command whose answers nest bracket labels, and by the schematic
  creators that render them.
-->

<!ENTITY DEPTH.roles "peer|child|grandchild">
<!ENTITY DEPTH.roles.count "3">
<!ENTITY DEPTH.max "5">
<!ENTITY DEPTH.mark.md "blockquote count: one greater-than per level">
<!ENTITY DEPTH.mark.nt "content count after the string tag, per SIGIL.nt.depth-in-content">
<!ENTITY DEPTH.refines "deeper is a refinement of its parent, never a restatement">

<!ENTITY LAW.DEPTH.1 "Depth encodes relation and nothing else: a peer stands beside, a child constrains, a grandchild specifies (DEPTH.roles); a level that neither constrains nor specifies is flattened to its parent.">
<!ENTITY LAW.DEPTH.2 "Depth never exceeds DEPTH.max levels; a chain that would nest deeper is rewritten as siblings under their nearest common parent, and the rewrite is stated.">
<!ENTITY LAW.DEPTH.3 "Each format marks depth its own way, DEPTH.mark.md in Markdown and DEPTH.mark.nt in NestedText; a depth readable in one rendering and lost in the other is a failed rendering.">
